Careful fix for fail-open without breaking dev: 
- If ADMIN_USER_IDS unset: allow only when NODE_ENV !== "production"; in production, deny with "Forbidden" (403) + clear message telling to set ADMIN_USER_IDS.
- isAdmin: same logic.

Risk: a production deployment without ADMIN_USER_IDS would suddenly get 403 on admin routes. That's the intended fail-closed fix. Add ADMIN_USER_IDS to .env.example with documentation. Check .env.example content for admin section.

